  "definition": "Mania is a state of unusually elevated excitement and overactivity, sometimes with psychotic features such as psychomotor agitation, inflated self-esteem, and rapidly shifting ideas. It is often linked with mental disorders such as cyclothymic disorder and bipolar disorders.",
